  "note": "CLAIM_CONFORMANCE checks mapping existing Capital read surfaces to the pinned read-model query draft docs/contracts/READ_MODEL_QUERIES.md (kix-protocol 7481b0e16ce9b903abbffa62249bb91cd9e63cfe, the vendor pin). Results are SIMULATED. Adapter mapping, stated honestly: the draft's get_credit_advance maps to the GET /api/state case views, which are literal CreditMachine.view dicts; get_credit_claim maps to the in-process CreditMachine.view_claim, since no dedicated HTTP route exists and GET /api/evidence rows are MockSettlement claims (the section-2.11 object), which section 2.13 forbids merging. No upstream query name is implemented and no route is added; this table prepares the parked read-model-credit-queries node only. Every check runs its read under the section-8 non-mutation guard (canonical_state, journal length, overlay state digest, operation_count). A missing protocol checkout is SKIPPED and is not a pass.",
